SDL2: the PowerVR screen is XRGB, not ARGB

The display shows no alpha, and a program that makes its textures in the
window's pixel format and fills them without alpha - Crispy Doom, whose
palette blit leaves it 0 - had them blended as fully transparent: it ran,
was heard, and showed black. SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB888, as desktop displays
report, makes such textures opaque.

ChaOS, for ports only (src/ports.h). After 0001 to 0006.

diff --git a/src/video/pvrfb/SDL_pvrfbvideo.c b/src/video/pvrfb/SDL_pvrfbvideo.c
index 787d11c..0d9a837 100644
--- a/src/video/pvrfb/SDL_pvrfbvideo.c
+++ b/src/video/pvrfb/SDL_pvrfbvideo.c
@@ -56,7 +56,11 @@ static int PVRFB_VideoInit(_THIS)
     SDL_zero(mode);
     mode.w = data->width;
     mode.h = data->height;
-    mode.format = data->bpp == 16 ? SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB565 : SDL_PIXELFORMAT_ARGB8888;
+    /* ChaOS: XRGB, as a desktop's display is: the screen shows no alpha,
+     * and a program that makes its textures in the window's format and
+     * fills them without one (Crispy Doom's palette blit leaves alpha 0)
+     * drew them fully transparent, and so black, with ARGB8888 */
+    mode.format = data->bpp == 16 ? SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB565 : SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB888;
     mode.refresh_rate = 60;
 
     SDL_zero(display);
